# GitHub Pages custom headers.
#
# One rule, deliberately: EVERY response revalidates (no-cache = use the
# cache but always re-check). This is the structural fix for the
# "two sites" bug — the bare URL serving a stale-cached index.html while
# ?intro=1 (a different cache key) fetched the fresh build. With HTML
# revalidated on every visit, a new deploy is visible immediately and
# exactly one version of the site can ever be served. Cost: 304s for
# unchanged hashed assets (no re-download).

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
